  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math> is molar heat capacity at constant pressure. Since the quantity is defined at constant pressure, it does not vary with pressure.<br>At higher temperatures, the rotational degree of freedom becomes active.<br>$C_P=\\frac{7}{2} R \\quad \\text { (Independent of } P \\text { ) }$<br>$\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{V}}=\\frac{5}{2} \\mathrm{R} \\quad \\text { (Independent of } \\mathrm{V} \\text { ) }$<br>$\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{V}}$ depends on $\\mathrm{T}$ and independent on $\\mathrm{V}$.<br>$\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}$ depends on $\\mathrm{T}$ and independent on $\\mathrm{P}$.",
